<h2 id="wmi-codes">World Manufacturer Identifier (Positions 1-3)</h2>

<p>The first three characters of every VIN make up the World Manufacturer Identifier (WMI). This globally standardized code tells you where the vehicle was manufactured and who built it. The WMI is assigned by the Society of Automotive Engineers (SAE) and coordinated internationally to prevent duplicates.</p>

