<h3>Position 2: Manufacturer</h3>

<p>The second character identifies the specific manufacturer. Combined with the first character, this narrows down the exact company that produced the vehicle.</p>

<h3>Position 3: Vehicle Type or Division</h3>

<p>The third character typically indicates the vehicle type (passenger car, truck, SUV) or the specific division within the manufacturer's organization. For example, General Motors uses different third characters for Chevrolet, Cadillac, and GMC vehicles.</p>

